From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:38:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(glm cuda): a tool call the end token left open is sent
 when it parses whole; a missing <arg_key> is put back

GLM-5.3-Flash sometimes writes its end token before </tool_call>. The CUDA server then sent no call: the
reply finished "stop" with the call's markup as its text, and agent clients stalled. When the model's end
token (not a stop string, not the token limit) ends the reply inside a GLM call, the call is now closed
(</arg_value> too when a value is open) and sent if it then parses strictly: one whole call to an offered
tool, nothing but its markup, arguments a JSON object (close_glm_call). Otherwise its markup stays the text,
as before. A call the token limit or a stop string cut is unchanged. Only models whose tokenizer has GLM's
call marks as tokens take this path.

GLM calls whose <arg_key> the model wrote as whitespace ("read path</arg_key><arg_value>..", or
"</arg_value>\npath</arg_key>") get it back in the shared GLM parser (repair_glm_keys), so both servers'
end parsers read them; before, the first form came back as text and the second lost the argument. Blocks
with no unopened </arg_key> are unchanged.

Reported on the GLM-5.3-Flash DGX Spark recipe, issue #22.

Tests: tests/test_glm_tool_call_end.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

